CCTPBridgeModule_Execute
├── when params length is less than 32 bytes
│   └── it should return failed result with "Invalid params encoding"
├── when amount is zero
│   └── it should return failed result with "Zero bridge amount"
├── when token is not USDC
│   └── it should return failed result with "Only USDC supported"
├── when destination domain is not configured
│   └── it should return failed result with "Domain not configured"
├── when maxFee is greater than or equal to amount
│   └── it should return failed result with "Max fee exceeds amount"
├── when caller has insufficient balance
│   └── it should return failed result with "Insufficient balance"
├── when token transfer from caller fails
│   └── it should return failed result with "Token transfer failed"
├── given domain configured without hook data
│   ├── when tokenMessenger reverts
│   │   └── it should revert (propagate CCTP revert)
│   └── when depositForBurn succeeds
│       ├── it should call depositForBurn on tokenMessenger with correct arguments
│       ├── it should revoke tokenMessenger approval after burn
│       ├── it should emit BridgeInitiated
│       └── it should return success result with (amount - maxFee) as amountOut
├── given domain configured with hook data
│   └── when depositForBurnWithHook succeeds
│       ├── it should call depositForBurnWithHook on tokenMessenger
│       ├── it should emit BridgeInitiated with hookData
│       └── it should return success result
├── given domain configured with standard finality
│   └── when bridge succeeds
│       └── it should pass minFinalityThreshold 2000 to tokenMessenger
├── when called by non-owner
│   └── it should succeed (execute is permissionless)
└── when amount equals maxFee plus one
    └── it should succeed with amountOut of 1
